        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-13T10:49:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure that I understand why we need all these pieces of state to know what to do with objects that have contents (buffers, textures, querysets). Won\u0027t we capture all the operations that may modify them, such that capturing their contents the first time that the `CaptureContext` sees them would be sufficient? This would handle the complexity mentioned here about the 2nd capture, as the CaptureContext should be reset for the second capture, and when `AddResource` is called, the object would be considered \"new\" for the capture and its contents captured.",
      "revId": "2f61752c7d75f9b588406cf301e79244127dc248",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3f0b4a7c_d23aa9b6",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/webgpu/RecordableObject.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 56,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003446
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-13T15:41:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Did you look at the tests? They don\u0027t pass without these. The tests should make it clear what they are for.\n\n\u003e Won\u0027t we capture all the operations that may modify them\n\nThere\u0027s nothing to capture with mapAsync. All we do is mark it as \"mNeedsCapture\" and the code automatically captures it **IF** it\u0027s used again.",
      "parentUuid": "98f81b30_25df1831",
      "revId": "2f61752c7d75f9b588406cf301e79244127dc248",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0b4d1b48_dba7ffd6",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/webgpu/RecordableObject.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 56,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-13T16:16:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[2]\n\nI did look at the tests (and I actually spent an hour reviewing this to try to understand why state was added). None of them do a map between two submits and as far as I can tell the current tests would pass with the suggested simplifications.\n\nIt makes sense that if we only track queue operations, then mapping wouldn\u0027t be visible in the trace. AFAIK it is the only non-queue operation that updates the contents of a resources, so WDYT of adding the data updates to the trace as a WriteBuffer in UnmapImpl instead? This way users will see the data uploads that they do and we avoid the need to track multiple additional booleans per recordable objects (that we have to statefully update in all the places in the backend that touch buffer/texture).",
      "parentUuid": "3f0b4a7c_d23aa9b6",
      "revId": "2f61752c7d75f9b588406cf301e79244127dc248",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ec36f420_a895ad3d",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/webgpu/RecordableObject.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 56,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003446
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-13T19:14:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think doing it unmapimpl is a distraction to the user. The buffer might not be used again even if they did update it. The current impl is \"on submit, upload all resources needed for the submit\".  The user can do map/unmap/map/unmap many times before submitting but we only need to capture once and only if the buffer is actually used.",
      "parentUuid": "0b4d1b48_dba7ffd6",
      "revId": "2f61752c7d75f9b588406cf301e79244127dc248",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f20afd4e_12065f79",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/webgpu/RecordableObject.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 56,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000685
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-13T21:04:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see the 2 approaches as:\n1. Record `buffer.unmap` as `queue.writeBuffer` inside `Buffer::UnmapImpl`. Capture gpu resource initial states once as first seen in capture context.\n2. Add states tracking to optimize recording of data updates by `buffer.unmap` (non-queue operation) and `clearBuffer` (initializing content)\n\n\n1 is the base line, basic and easy implementation.\n2 is the one-step further optimization implementation taking into account things like avoiding reading of unused unmapped buffer, and uninteresting initial 0s. But more error-prone with states managing.\n\n2.1 specializing initializing recording:\n 2.1.1 `clearBuffer` as Corentin pointed out it can set only a subset range so we should view them as unspecialized write operation.\n 2.1.2 empty render target texture: How can we tell if it\u0027s empty, if there\u0027s copy*ToTexture outside of capture context? Or render pass scissor rects + clear value. It seems there are many ways to make this dirty and it\u0027d be hard to track if we need to set `mHasData` to every places. I agree we can check [`Texture::IsInitialized`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/Texture.h;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d1?q\u003dTextureBase%20f:dawn\u0026ss\u003dchromium). If it\u0027s false, we don\u0027t readback. Otherwise we just read back the initial value of the texture.\n\n\n2.2 avoid buffer with many unmap calls but unused.\n(I never forsee this far.) Great we think about this and make the optimization that only 1 readback at most, with one state.",
      "parentUuid": "ec36f420_a895ad3d",
      "revId": "2f61752c7d75f9b588406cf301e79244127dc248",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "64b45c57_69d00898",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/webgpu/RecordableObject.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 56,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003446
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-13T21:42:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "capturing at unmap really doesn\u0027t make sense given the design. We only capture buffers used on the `queue`. A buffer never used on the queue, from the POV of capture, doesn\u0027t exist, but the user can still map and unmap it.",
      "parentUuid": "f20afd4e_12065f79",
      "revId": "2f61752c7d75f9b588406cf301e79244127dc248",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cff1a4d4_baaf75c8",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/webgpu/RecordableObject.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 56,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-14T13:34:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah that\u0027s all very confusing. When I read \"buffers used on a queue\" my expectation was that the trace wouldn\u0027t record unused resources, but would record all the mutating operations that happen so as to be able to replay it (everything is on the queue except the mapping, and maybe in the future the bindgroup updates). If we think it is confusing to the user, we can hide it in a future UI. For the tracing, I would imagine that it would make the recording simpler (in the way this thread is about), and would likely avoid recording redundant data in the trace.\n\nWDYT of discussing this in the weekly meeting tomorrow if we don\u0027t find a resolution by then?",
      "parentUuid": "64b45c57_69d00898",
      "revId": "2f61752c7d75f9b588406cf301e79244127dc248",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
